      "extract": "Yet another left coideal subalgebra of U is G−, an obvious quantum analog of U(n−). In this section, we consider coideal subalgebras of G− which cor- respond to classical enveloping algebras of Lie subalgebra s of n− and related Lie subalgebras of g. Most of the results presented here are from [Ke]. Let π′ be a subset of the simple roots π of g. There are a number of Lie subalgebras of g which can be associated to",
